        "fullVisibleText": "Faculty Profiles Back to Faculty Profiles Yu Qiao Professor, SE Thermodynamics, advanced energy-related materials, high-performance infrastructure materials, in-situ resource utilization, smart materials and structures, failure analysis for engineering materials and structures. Capsule Bio: Yu Qiao received a bachelor's degree in applied mechanics from the University of Science and Technology of China in 1994, and a master's degree in materials science from the Chinese Academy of Sciences in 1997. He received a Ph.D. in mechanical engineering from MIT in 2002. From 2002-2006, he was an assistant professor at the University of Akron. He joined UCSD in 2006. Education: Ph.D. in Mechanical Engineering, Massachusetts Institute of Technology, Cambridge, Massachusetts (2002) Update your profile Email: yqiao@ucsd.edu Office Phone: 858-534-3388 Lab Website Institute Affiliations: Charles Lee Powell Structural Research Laboratories",
